There's a pretty hilarious side effect of from how spell book gifts are
generated - If you read the book you know the spell and then the game
tries to avoid giving you another one just like it.  If you do not read
the book then that type stays in the list of books the game considers
worth giving you.

For a character at XP=N the game tries N times to give you a book you do
not know in a school you do know.  For character at XP=30 that's a lot
of tries before it falls back to a completely random generation.

One game I ended up with several plain spell books before I read through
the source code to figure out what was happening.  I read one of them
and didn't get another.


